# ============================================================================
# FaniDex / Minecraft Webstore — Frontend Environment Configuration
# ============================================================================
#
# The frontend currently requires NO build-time environment variables.
# API calls are made to a relative "/api/v1" path:
#   - In development, Vite's dev server proxies "/api" -> http://localhost:8080
#     (see vite.config.ts). Just run the backend on port 8080 alongside `npm run dev`.
#   - In production, the included Nginx config (nginx.conf) proxies "/api/" to the
#     "backend" container/service. Adjust `proxy_pass` there if your backend runs
#     elsewhere.
#
# This file is kept as a placeholder for future configuration (e.g. a custom
# VITE_API_BASE_URL) and so tooling that expects an .env.example is satisfied.
# If you introduce Vite env vars, remember: only variables prefixed with
# VITE_ are exposed to client-side code (import.meta.env.VITE_*).
#
# Example (not currently used by the app):
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api/v1
